A misty Irish hillside at twilight, ancient standing stones arranged in a circle silhouetted against a deep orange and purple sky. Translucent, ethereal figures of ancestors drift between the stones, their forms swirling like smoke merging with the fog. In the foreground, a harvest scene with golden wheat sheaves and autumn gourds scattered near a Celtic spiral carved into weathered rock. The brushwork captures thick, swirling patterns in the sky reminiscent of turbulent energy, with bold impasto strokes creating movement in the clouds and ghostly figures. Rich autumnal colors dominate—burnt sienna, deep violet, cadmium yellow—applied with visible passionate brushstrokes. The standing stones glow with an inner warmth while the spirits shimmer in cool blues and greens, creating a boundary between worlds. Stars emerge in the darkening sky, rendered as luminous halos of light. Style of Vincent van Gogh.
